the boulder, but in vain.\" That means pushing the boulder LEFT from (39,10) to (37,10) failed because (37,10) is solid stone.\n\nAnd when I tried to push UP from (38,11) to (38,10), pushing the boulder to (38,9), it failed because (38,9) is blank (solid stone).\n\nSo the boulder is surrounded by:\n- (37,10): solid stone (left)\n- (38,9): solid stone (up)\n- (39,10): corridor (right) - this is the direction I push FROM, not TO\n- (38,11): corridor (down) - this is where I'm standing\n\nThe boulder can't be pushed in any direction:\n- Push left: (37,10) is solid stone\n- Push right: would need to be at (37,10) to push right, but (37,10) is solid stone\n- Push up: (38,9) is solid stone\n- Push down: would need to be at (38,9) to push down, but (38,9) is solid stone\n\nWait, I'm confused. To push the boulder RIGHT, I need to be at (37,10) (left of the boulder) and move right. The boulder would move from (38,10) to (39,10). But (37,10) is solid stone, so I can't get there.\n\nTo push the boulder DOWN, I need to be at (38,9) (above the boulder) and move down. The boulder would move from (38,10) to (38,11). But (38,9) is solid stone, so I can't get there.\n\nTo push the boulder UP, I need to be at (38,11) (below the boulder, where I am) and move up. The boulder would move from (38,10) to (38,9). But (38,9) is solid stone, so the boulder can't move there. This is what I tried and it failed.\n\nTo push the boulder LEFT, I need to be at (39,10) (right of the boulder) and move left. The boulder would move from (38,10) to (37,10). But (37,10) is solid stone, so the boulder can't move there. This is what I tried earlier and it failed.\n\nSo the boulder is completely stuck! It can't be pushed in any direction because all the adjacent tiles (except where I can stand) are solid stone.\n\nThis means the boulder is NOT blocking a corridor to the stairs down. It's just a boulder in a dead-end corridor.\n\nOK, I need to completely rethink my approach. I've been on level 2 for almost 1