        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The game server infrastructure has become unstable - the state endpoint authentication has expired. Let me provide my final summary.\n\n**Final Progress Report:**\n\n**Best Achievement: Dungeon Level 2 (Dlvl: 2, Turn ~422)**\n\nAcross multiple game sessions, I attempted to descend as deep as possible into the NetHack dungeon:\n\n**First Game (Original Server):**\n- Started as a Valkyrie on Level 1\n- Explored Level 1, found stairs down, and descended to Level 2\n- On Level 2, found stairs down at (43,4) behind a hidden door at (42,5)\n- Got stuck: boulders blocked the corridor leading to the stairs down room\n- The pathfinding tool hung trying to push unpushable boulders (a known defect documented in the game's `stall_watchdog.py`)\n- The stall watchdog killed the game server after 300+ seconds of no progress\n\n**Subsequent Attempts:**\n- Manually restarted game servers twice\n- In one attempt, found stairs down on Level 1 at (54,5) but couldn't reach it (no valid path)\n- Servers repeatedly crashed due to the same pathfinding bug\n- State endpoint authentication eventually expired, making further play impossible\n\n**Items Collected:** Gold, elven leather helm, scroll labeled READ ME, potions, gems\n**Monsters Killed:** Grid bugs, goblins, newts\n**Levels Reached:** Dungeon Level 2\n\nI was unable to retrieve the Amulet of Yendor or escape the dungeon. The primary blocker was a known pathfinding bug in the game server's `nethack_bfs` module that causes infinite hangs when the pathfinder encounters boulder-blocked corridors, eventually crashing the server with no recovery mechanism.",
